{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are such that the graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db50fb18d8162fa7ae542c19d4d0bb553bc6b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=ax+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc0f5b90e821897add7f6b6aa4aed4dec34f3404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3x+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> intersect the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis at the same point. What is the sum of all possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinates of these points of intersection?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cabf2c6ac3170c99dfb040eaf80a29846c9335b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ {-20}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ {-18}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ {-15}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ {-12}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ {-8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"455\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values of the equations should be equal by the problem statement. We have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b5974079f962de0b0cdffd7cc3e068e6aa9753a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 = ax + 5 \\implies x = -\\dfrac{5}{a}\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05ddc94c34a7ca9558c5927b090cbe03dbd143a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 = 3x+b \\implies x= -\\dfrac{b}{3}\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"37\" />\nWhich means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a816e2e78ddb95d2446fe65f792d4d65d844642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\dfrac{5}{a} = -\\dfrac{b}{3} \\implies ab = 15\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"37\" />\nThe only possible pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> then are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1537eb1bbd18d22a3c188acbfe04ae298bed0d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b) = (1,15), (3,5), (5,3), (15, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />. These pairs give respective <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5145f5141f8ec693122b501e7635d13e275e7884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5, -\\dfrac{5}{3}, -1, -\\dfrac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"37\" /> which have a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c58e9556b419cfddcd94fb2d1fe47d84c45483f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\: -8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using a part of what we got from Solution 1, we notice that the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a526e44e36254c196af103613bc724f312b6a209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. We also know for the first equation that the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divided by something. Furthermore, for the second equation, the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83b80e6c45d8277f7b005f829f5b2aabbd7e227f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac13,-\\frac23,-\\frac33, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"125\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, we see that, the only values common between the two sequences are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/4391f97d9abd0ba70eb87b9aa8e6083f2e77b746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1, -5, -\\frac13,-\\frac53$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"37\" />, and adding them up, we get our final answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c58e9556b419cfddcd94fb2d1fe47d84c45483f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\: -8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uUxcMZVFSR8?si=zQWytkiPOVw1CRTG\">https://youtu.be/uUxcMZVFSR8?si=zQWytkiPOVw1CRTG</a> ~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-vZKwIazT08&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvKEM8u4Q-7Gi0rU5WU4WOb1&amp;index=1\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-vZKwIazT08&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvKEM8u4Q-7Gi0rU5WU4WOb1&amp;index=1</a> - AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikita